From 03c8d3086e08b0af60e8104f1c59cf639ab74a91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:37:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): stop React #310 blanking the product screen

Opening a product cold crashed the app with React error #310, "Rendered
more hooks than during the previous render", and left a blank page with no
way back.

ProductPage rendered <Spinner /> while the workspace loaded (12 hooks) and
returned early when the product was missing, then called useState useState
useEffect once the product arrived (15 hooks). React counts hooks per
component, so the second render threw.

- Move the loading and not-found guards into a thin ProductPage route shell
  and render <ProductContent key={product.id} />, so the component that owns
  hooks always runs all of them.
- Add RouteError and wire it as errorElement on the root and Layout routes.
  A page that throws now degrades inside the shell instead of unmounting the
  app; navigation and the session stay usable.
- Add tools/react-lint (rules-of-hooks over apps/web/src) and run it in CI.
  Its toolchain is outside the workspaces because it pins TypeScript 5;
  typescript-eslint cannot parse with the workspace's TypeScript 7 yet.
- Add a jsdom mount test that renders the loading state and then the data.
  It is the only renderer whose hook list survives between renders, so it is
  the test that actually reproduces #310: it fails on the old code.
- Assert the product screen in project-workflow-smoke.

Verified: typecheck, 58 web tests (43+99+57+58 across workspaces), lint:hooks
and the production build all pass.
